I've written the session plan: two task files plus the issue responses. The commit didn't happen because session_plan/ is in .gitignore, so git add refused it. The plan command ends in || true, so the harness seems to expect that, and the files are on disk.

Task 1 — Fixes #1026 (product, self-driven). This finishes item 1 of the decision @yuanhao wrote on the ticket ("Add the note to json and stream-json output too"). The exit-code half landed on Day 250.
• `--output-format json`: the result object gets a stop-reason field: normal end, output limit (saying whether the user or a default set it), or refusal. is_error should match the exit code; right now a cut or refused run can exit 1 while reporting is_error: false.
• `stream-json`: it gets the same stderr note the text path prints, reusing the existing wording. stdout stays pure JSON lines.
• Tests: they run the real binary against the stub cases Day 250 already added to tests/print_stdout_contract.rs, plus a positive control and the docs updates.

Task 2 — Fixes #1143 (product). This is the backlog-drain slot, since there are 13 open self-filed issues and this one has the least work left.
• GIF: I chose option (a), refusing GIF in /add, @path and --image. yoagent 0.27.1's own read_file already refuses it, so yoyo currently accepts a file with one hand and refuses it with the other. The cost: Anthropic users lose GIF attachments; the refusal will tell them to convert to PNG.
• Already wrong: the --image error (src/cli.rs:2737) and the help line (src/help.rs:110) still list bmp, which was removed from the format list earlier. The task makes both messages come from the one list.

